<title>DUBAI: Saudi gold mine produces 2,600 kg in '96.</title>
<headline>Saudi gold mine produces 2,600 kg in '96.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's second largest gold mine, Sukhaybarat, produced some 2,600 kg of the metal last year, managing director Per-Martin Sandgren said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We produced around 2,600 kg,&quot; Sandgren told Reuters by telephone from the mine, some 750 km northeast of the Red Sea port city of Jeddah.</p>
<p>The mine -- a joint venture between Saudi Precious Metals Co and Boliden Mineral Aktiebolag, a unit of Trelleborg -- produced 2,826 kg in 1995.</p>
</text>
